# Agent/AI Configuration (local development only)
# NOTE: agent-workflow/ and .github/workflows/ are intentionally NOT ignored:
# agent-workflow/ is the shared, repo-owned coordination layer that all
# agents/models are expected to read and update (see
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-11-agent-workflow-design.md), and
# .github/workflows/ holds the actual CI definitions, which must be tracked
# for GitHub Actions to run at all.
# AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md stay tracked as the canonical, short entry-point
# pointers (both just point to agent-workflow/START-HERE.md). Every other
# per-tool adapter below carries a full duplicate copy of the same guidance
# for tools that can't load a shared skill, and is dev-local only.
.github/*
!.github/workflows/
.claude/
.agents/
.agent/
.jules/
.gemini/
.augment/
.clinerules/
.continue/
.cursor/
.kilocode/
.kiro/
.openhands/
.roo/
.trae/
.windsurf/
.junie/
.hermes/
.rules
.goosehints
CONVENTIONS.md
GEMINI.md
QWEN.md
WARP.md
replit.md
skills/
graphify-out/
.vscode/
memories/

